  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Capacity Building for Namibian Civil Society</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This action titled `&lt;em&gt;Comprehensive Capacity Building for Namibian Civil Society&#xbf;&lt;/em&gt; is aligned with the `Measures in Favour of Civil Society&#xbf; detailed in Section 3.1 of the European Union&apos;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1GCHA_en__1182__1182&amp;cs=0&amp;amp;sca_esv=466299774e926d41&amp;amp;q=Multi-annual+Indicative+Programme+%28MIP%29&amp;amp;sa=X&amp;amp;ved=2ahUKEwip8MjKsbqQAxUBi_0HHTY9BfIQxccNegQIAhAB&amp;amp;mstk=AUtExfA3BJg1UbgLTFlujuFpKXXR5dfC2D14bx7l9mSx7ecCwOY-b8sTir5-GA9M2-RDrzHmGmcz9uJIkcGrMikhW2BWbZQLLYZTZY47UpYmS53-alAPXYXdi52rT_ayD-my8SM&amp;amp;csui=3&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; style=&quot;color: windowtext;&quot;&gt;Multi-Annual Indicative Programme (MIP)&lt;/a&gt; for Namibia (2021-2027), this service contract is financed under the Annual Action Plan in favour of the Republic of Namibia for 2023&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The services comprised of trainings, technical assistance and three studies aim to enhance the participation, engagement, and advocacy capacity of Civil Society Organisations (CSOs) in defining and implementing the country&#xbf;s development agenda, with a specific emphasis on inclusive green growth and governance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Global objective: To strengthen the role Civil Society Organisations as an independent actor in democratic governance and Namibias economic development agenda.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Specific objectives&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I.Building civil society organisations capacity for policy dialogue, evidence-based advocacy, coalition-building and citizen representation to strengthen democratic governance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;II.Promoting the long-term sustainability of Namibia&apos;s civil society sector through strengthened organisational operations, management practises, diversified financing, and human resource development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;III.Building civil society organisations capacity as an informed stakeholder in Namibia&apos;s economic transformation, with technical capacity to engage on energy, green industrialisation, and extractive resource governance.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
